Known non-deterministic corruption in the ARM64 build of z3-4.3.1: on
this test the solver process sometimes closes its output stream
mid-check-sat with no response at all ("Error writing to solver: ...
NoResponseException: Solver process closed its output stream without a
response"), rather than the "unexpected character" truncation seen on
other tests affected by this bug. An earlier CI capture instead produced
a clean-looking "Failed to check-sat" error, captured in the now-
superseded .tst.out.z3-4.3.linux-arm64.bad / .tst.err.z3-4.3.linux-arm64.bad
goldens -- the difference between the two captures against the identical
binary confirms the non-determinism, so a .bad golden (exact-match) can
never stay in sync with this output and this test is skipped instead.
Never seen on x64.
See https://github.com/smtlib/jSMTLIB/issues/101 for the broader ARM64
z3-4.3.1 correctness-bug tracking issue.
